      "content": "While mild gas pain can sometimes be managed with over-the-counter medication and rest, a dull ache that shifts location and persists for hours could indicate early signs of appendicitis or another serious condition. Because abdominal pain that moves or worsens requires prompt evaluation, it is significantly safer to visit a doctor or urgent care immediately rather than waiting to see if it gets better. Please do not take ibuprofen immediately if there is any chance of internal bleeding or if you do not know the cause of the pain, as this could mask important symptoms. Your health is the priority here, so getting a professional medical assessment is the best course of action.",
